WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.390
This is a long-lasting insecticide-treated
bed net.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:11.590
When used correctly, it has been shown to
reduce deaths by 20% for children under 5.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:17.880
It costs just one dollar and sixty six cents,
or about 30% less than the cheapest coffee

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.330
at Starbucks.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.810
That’s the thing about extreme poverty.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:29.010
The poorer someone is, the simpler, easier,
and cheaper are the immediate remedies.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:34.880
Life-saving vaccines and high-yield seeds
cost just pennies each when bought in bulk.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:41.921
Yet, in the past 60 years, the rich world
has collectively given $3.5 trillion in development

00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:44.330
aid to poor countries.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:50.200
The Marshall Plan, by contrast, cost 150 billion
in today’s dollars.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.870
So, where has all this money gone?

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.450
Why does a problem for which we’ve devoted
so many trillions of dollars and know of cheap

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.600
solutions to, remain?

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.890
The obvious and seductive answer is corruption.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:10.979
Aid, we’re told, ends up in the hands of
dictators, who spend it on palaces, leopard

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:14.159
skin hats, and Lamborghinis.

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:20.049
If only this money actually reached the people
who need it, these problems would simply disappear.

00:01:20.049 --> 00:01:22.979
…But would they?

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:29.060
How do we know that corruption, itself a very
real issue, isn’t hiding an even bigger

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.320
one?

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.549
How do we know, in other words, that when
foreign aid does reach the intended recipients,

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:38.659
it produces the desired results?

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:41.840
The only way to find out for sure would be
an experiment.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:48.139
And to dispel such an intuitive assumption,
it would have to be impeccable — staffed

00:01:48.139 --> 00:01:54.189
by the world’s foremost experts, supported
by many millions of dollars, and untarnished

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:57.009
by ulterior motives.

00:01:57.009 --> 00:02:05.729
As it turns out, such an experiment was conducted
— for 10 years, starting in 2005…

